# The entire ~/.claude dir is co-managed by the Claude Code runtime + agent
# environment (settings, enabledPlugins, hooks, plugin state, caches, transcripts
# are all rewritten at runtime). Tracking it caused recurring `chezmoi update`
# conflicts, so the whole directory is left unmanaged.
#
# Exception: ~/.claude/rules/*.md holds portable, machine-independent instructions
# that Claude Code loads at user scope. Nothing rewrites them at runtime, so they
# are safe to track. Re-including a child needs the parent glob (`.claude/*`) and
# an explicit un-ignore of each directory on the way down; a bare `.claude` ignore
# cannot be negated.
.claude/*
!.claude/rules
.claude/rules/*
!.claude/rules/*.md
